response:
 From noon to 3 p.m., the hour hand completes 3/2 = 1.5 "full revolutions" (360 degrees clockwise), which is 3/2(2 pi) = 3 pi radians.

\begin{align*}
\text{Distance traveled by the tip of the hour hand at noon to 3 p.m.} &= \text{1.5 full revolutions}\\
& \times\chunk{the length of the hour hand}\\
&= 6 \times 3\pi \text{ inches}\\
\end{align*}

From noon to 3 p.m., the minute hand completes 3 twists (360 degrees clockwise), which is \(3 \times 2 \pi = 6\pi\) radians.

\begin{align*}
\text{Distance traveled by the tip of the minute hand at noon to  3 p.m.} &= \text{3 twists}\\
& \times\chunk{the length of the minute hand}\\
&= 8 \times 6\pi \text{ inches}\\
\end{align*}

Thus, the ratio is \(\ \frac{3\pi \times 6}{3\pi \times 8} = \boxed{\frac{3}{4}}\缩短计 as fractions. </think> <answer> \frac{3}{4} </answer>

